  m_Text: 'Small predatory arthropods swim among large clusters of sponges.


    Although corals had evolved by the time the Cambrian came around, they were rare
    in number compared to the diversity of sponges. Instead of the coral reefs, the
    Cambrian had Sponge reefs. '
